Three blocks are in contact with each other, and they are at rest on a horizontal surface with negligible friction. The masses of the blocks are $2\ \mathrm{kg}$, $4\ \mathrm{kg}$, and $1\ \mathrm{kg}$, as shown in the figure. While a force of $28\ \mathrm{N}$ pushes the $2\ \mathrm{kg}$ block to the right, what is the magnitude of the force that the $2\ \mathrm{kg}$ block exerts on the $4\ \mathrm{kg}$ block?

